  "releaseNotes": "2.0.0:\n- LibSass, the default, now fails with an error on @use and @forward (the module system of Dart Sass), on the line of the rule. It wrote them to the CSS without an error, so the CSS was broken; a build that passed with such a file now fails. Set \"runtime\": \"DartSass\" for the file in sassconfig.json.\n- Visual Studio: Sass Compiler › Initialize with sets up an ASP.NET Core or Blazor project with an empty Sass file (LibSass or Dart Sass), Bulma 0.9.4 or 1.0.4, Bootstrap 5.3.9, or Pico CSS 2.1.1. The framework is downloaded with LibMan into Styles/lib and listed in libman.json. Bulma comes with styles for ASP.NET Core validation, and a Blazor project gets the Blazor error and loading styles.\n- Visual Studio: Sass Compiler › Add icon font adds Font Awesome, Material Symbols or Bootstrap Icons, with a CopyWebFonts target in the project file that copies the fonts to wwwroot/fonts before the build.\n- Visual Studio: Sass Compiler › Cleanup VS template moves what the ASP.NET Core templates put in wwwroot (lib, and the .css, .js and .map files) to the Recycle Bin.\n- Visual Studio: the Sass Compiler menu of a project is below Manage NuGet Packages and Manage Client-Side Libraries.",
